+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Zero Intensity Max:** If an energy volume has a maximum intensity of 0, division by zero occurs in the ratio calculation [S1, unofficial]. The implementation guards against this with a check `if intensity_max > 0` [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Magnitude Volume Zeros:** If the magnitude volume sample is 0, no energy blending occurs for that voxel, and the color remains black/transparent unless handled by the compositing alpha [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Step Size Artifacts:** Using a large step size (20) for interactive mode may cause aliasing or missed thin structures [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Coordinate System Assumption:** The source implementation adds world-space view vectors to voxel-space volume center coordinates, assuming the view matrix scales to voxel units or the coordinate system is normalized [S1, unofficial]. Arbitrary camera origins require modifying the coordinate formula [G].
+*   **Clamping Bug:** The source code compares the pre-scaled float value to 255 before flooring; the corrected implementation clamps the final scaled integer to 255 to prevent overflow [G].
